# RRS/XCO2 workflow products are reproducible and can be large or actively
# updated during remote runs. Keep source/configuration/provenance in Git and
# force-add only small reference tables that form part of the documented input.
#
# PRIVACY BOUNDARY: manuscripts and locally collected resources are maintained
# outside this public repository under ~/RRS_XCO2. Never stage either tree,
# including with `git add -f` (the repository pre-commit guard also rejects it).
**/RRS_XCO2/resources/
**/RRS_XCO2/manuscript/
# Private research handoffs belong in ~/RRS_XCO2/private_notes, not Git.
TODO/PRIVATE_*
**/species_rayleigh_raman_todo.md
# Host/account-specific institutional runbooks are private operational notes.
RRS_XCO2/inversion/for_gattaca.md
# Host/account-specific Gattaca operational runbooks remain private working
# notes.  Keep portable source launchers and tests tracked separately.
RRS_XCO2/inversion/GATTACA_TAPERED_SIF_RETRIEVALS.md
